    "Performance gate baseline (PRD AOS-23.2): the metrics tools/perf/compare.mjs tracks and their reference values.",
    "Each metric: file = basename of the results file the MEDLEVO_PERF suites write (apps/server/test/perf -> <scenario>.json, e2e/perf.spec.ts -> desktop.json); path = JSON path inside its \"results\" ([field=value] selects array elements, several matches are summed); better = lower | higher; floor = absolute change (same unit) below which a difference is noise and never fails.",
    "SEEDED, PROVISIONAL: the values are the R1-c numbers of docs/academic-os/PHASE1_REPORT.md §7 / docs/PERFORMANCE.md «GATE-1» (server: medians of 3 runs; browser: one run), measured on a 4-vCPU Linux VM, not on GitHub hardware. They are not comparable with a GitHub runner (nor with a laptop), so while provisional is true the gate reports and never fails.",
    "TO RE-RECORD from a CI run on GitHub hardware: download the perf-results artifact of the CI perf job and either copy its baseline.candidate.json over this file or run `node tools/perf/compare.mjs --runs-root <artifact dir> --record`; review the diff and commit it. Recording sets provisional to false: from then on a regression > threshold_pct fails the job unless docs/perf/accepted-regressions.json lists it with a reason.",
    "value null = nothing recorded yet (no R1-c number maps to it unambiguously): reported, never fails, filled by --record."
  ],
